## 2. Method (declared readings)
- mutmut 3.8.1 model (read from THIS version's source, not guessed flags): `mutmut run
  reads config from CWD (setup.cfg [mutmut]); copies source + also_copy paths into
  ./mutants/ and mutates ONLY the copy — the repo's real files are never written;
  tests run with cwd=mutants/. Repo porcelain is therefore structurally untouched by
  the run (verified, §6).
- Scope config lives in SCRATCH only: /tmp/gw-mutmut-scratch/run-hyg/setup.cfg and
  /tmp/gw-mutmut-scratch/run-static/setup.cfg (source_paths = src/check_hygiene.py /
  server/static_app.py via symlink farm; nothing added to the repo — card requirement).
- Module-path association: mutmut keys mutants by file path (tools/check_hygiene.py ->
  tools.check_hygiene) while tests import the top-level names. Declared scratch fix:
  hygiene farm places the file at src/check_hygiene.py (mutmut strips the src. prefix
  so keys == check_hygiene.*, matching the tests' `import check_hygiene`), and the
  static-app harness imports it as `from server import static_app` (the path-derived
  key). Without this, mutmut 3.8.1 aborts with its own association guard (seen live).
- Hygiene test universe (declared reading of the card's 'hygiene test universe'): the
  pure-Python files that import tools/check_hygiene and exercise it IN-PROCESS:
  tests/test_purity.py, test_bridge_contract.py, test_data_schemas.py,
  test_loot_structure.py, test_economy_numbers.py, test_heroes.py, test_enemy_walk.py
  (122 tests, green in 7.6s). The engine-tier files reuse blank_code incidentally for
  their own greps and would add minutes of godot-probe runtime per stats pass without
  covering any new gate function; test_scaffold.py drives the gate ONLY via subprocess
  (see LIMITS) and its gate-green leg is additionally structurally incompatible with
  the trampoline world (the copy legitimately exceeds the gate's own 400-line ceiling),
  so it is excluded from the mutation universe and runs in the untouched full suite.
- static_app universe: tests/test_served.py + the two test_scaffold server legs run
  clean-run guards (they exercise the shipped HTTP shape in the copy world), and the
  SCORED association comes from a SCRATCH-ONLY direct harness (tests_scratch/
  test_direct_static_app.py, 15 tests, mock handler + tmp docroots) because the repo
  suite reaches static_app only through a subprocess server, which mutmut 3.8.1 cannot
  associate (in-process recording only) — DECLARED: the static_app kill-rate measures
  the direct harness, and that gap in the repo suite is itself finding F-3.
- Harness sealed before use (negative-testing rule): the scratch direct harness runs
  15 GREEN on the clean copy, and went RED (7 failed) when the escape guard in the
  COPY's static_app.py was planted-broken (commonpath != -> ==):
  `7 failed, 8 passed` — red output kept at §7.

