### 5b. tools/check_hygiene.py — 173 survivors

The structural cause behind almost all of them, stated once (FINDING F-1): the
in-process hygiene universe asserts ABSENCE only (no banned token in blanked code,
zero raw hits in scans). The shipped .gd/.py corpus is clean BY DESIGN, so blanking
that misfires, empties itself, or skips whole comment families stays green — a
mutation kill needs a POSITIVE CONTROL (a fixture that MUST be blanked / MUST trip).
Second cause (FINDING F-2): blank_code is only ever run with family="gd" in-process;
the gate blanks py (triple-quote), js (backtick), css, cfg (';') and html ('<!--')
against the shipped tree, and no in-process test blanks any of those families.

HARMLESS equivalents (8): blank_code nxt-value mutants 6/7/14 (the value flows only
into =="/" / =="*" comparisons and can never equal either; 3); words 2/3 (the camel
regex re-tokenizes any unsplit part, so the split delimiter is unobservable; 2);
read 8 (utf-8 == UTF-8; 1); tripwire_hit 22/23 (phrase-window ±1: out-of-range slices
cannot equal the token list; 2).

Timeouts (12, blank_code loop guards) are NOT survivors: mutmut scores them killed-
side; they are loop-guard inversions that hang — a real behavior change, detected as
timeout. Listed for completeness: 105, 107, 199, 200, 39, 43, 44, 52, 70, 74, 75, 90

