### 5c. FINDING ROWS (test-gaps routed to the orchestrator, not silently accepted)
- F-1 (P2, TEST-GAP): the in-process hygiene universe has NO POSITIVE CONTROL for
  blank_code / walk / tripwire identifier-mode / rel. One synthetic fixture per branch
  (a gd text with #, //, /* */ and a comment-EOF case; a data identifier that MUST trip
  'shop' and 'cash_store'; a scan assertion of coverage-count > 0) would kill the bulk
  of the 150+ surviving mutants. Evidence: condition-INVERSIONS survive (blank_code 15-
  23, walk 2/7/12) — a scan that returns NOTHING stays green.
- F-2 (P3, TEST-GAP): js/html/css/cfg/py blanking families are never exercised
  in-process; the gate uses them on the shipped tree. Family-scoped fixture set needed.
- F-3 (P3, TEST-GAP): server/static_app.py has NO in-process test — the repo reaches it
  only via a subprocess server, which mutmut cannot associate; without the scratch
  direct harness the module scores 0/121 by association alone. Sub-finding F-3a (P3):
  serve()'s OSError branch is untested at EVERY tier (11 survivors).
- F-4 (P3, TEST-GAP): _resolve lstrip("/") boundary — add a request path like
  /xhr.js to test_served/test_purity negative rows.
- F-5 (P4, host fact): python3 -m venv is broken on VM350 (ensurepip/python3.10-venv
  missing); virtualenv works — worth fixing fleet-wide for other cards.
- NOT a finding, declared boundary: check_hygiene.main() mutants (234) are not scoreable
  by mutmut (subprocess driver). Their live substitute already ships: test_scaffold.py
  proves the gate GREEN on the tree and RED on a planted bad file, inside the full
  suite run above (287 green) — the declared substitute for main(), honest-limit row.

